  data:
    Id: a-b-testing
    Term: A/B Testing
    Abbreviation: 
    Category: 7
    Difficulty: 1
    ShortDefinition: Comparing two or more variants with live players to measure
      which performs better.
    SimpleExplanation: Show different versions to different players and keep the
      winner.
    WhyItMatters: A/B tests replace opinion wars with evidence for design and monetization
      changes.
    Example: Half of new users see a shorter tutorial; retention and completion are
      compared.
    CommonMistake: Calling a change validated after too small a sample or too short
      a window.
    PracticePrompt: Define a primary metric and minimum sample size before launching
      one experiment.
    GameUses:
    - Onboarding experiments
    - Store UX
    - Economy tuning
    RelatedTermIds:
    - playtesting
    - retention
    - conversion-rate
    - cohort-analysis
    Tags:
    - analytics
    - experiments
    - qa
    Synonyms: []
